 Step 9: Commands for the OFFLINE PC
  Once you plug the USB into the air-gapped PC, follow this sequence in a standard terminal (Command Prompt or PowerShell):

  1. Extract the Environment:

   1 mkdir C:\doc_parser_env
   2 tar -xzf E:\doc_parser_env.tar.gz -C C:\doc_parser_env
   3 # (Change E: to your USB drive letter)

  2. Set Offline Path Variables (Tells the code where the USB models are):
  Note: If you copy the AI_Cache to the offline PC's D: drive, use D: below.

   1 set HF_HOME="E:\AI_Cache\huggingface"
   2 set DOCLING_MODELS_CACHE="E:\AI_Cache\docling"
   3 set EASYOCR_MODULE_PATH="E:\AI_Cache\easyocr"

  3. Activate and Run:

   1 # Activate
   2 C:\doc_parser_env\Scripts\activate.bat
   3
   4 # Go to code and launch
   5 cd E:\Zenith-Vault
   6 streamlit run app.py --browser.gatherUsageStats False
